# Auth & Security

## Clerk Integration

- **Mobile**: Use `@clerk/clerk-expo` with token cache via `expo-secure-store`
- **Backend**: Use `@clerk/nextjs` middleware for route protection
- All API routes (except webhooks and health) require authentication
- User sync: Clerk webhook (`user.created`, `user.updated`, `user.deleted`) syncs to Supabase users table
- Webhook verification: Always verify Svix headers before processing

## PII & Medical Data

- **Never log** patient health information (PHI) - filter before sending to Sentry
- Prescriptions, consultation notes, and medical data are sensitive
- RLS policies ensure users can only access their own data
- File uploads (documents, prescriptions) use private Supabase buckets
- Delete sensitive data on user deletion (CASCADE in database)

## Security Headers

- API CORS is restricted to the mobile app origin
- Clerk handles JWT-based session management
- Server-side operations use service role key (never expose to client)

## Environment Variables

- Never commit `.env` files
- Use `.env.example` as documentation
- Prefixes: `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for Next.js client, `EXPO_PUBLIC_` for Expo
- Secrets: `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY`, `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`, `DAILY_API_KEY`, `RESEND_API_KEY`

## Input Validation

- Always validate on both client AND server
- Use shared Zod schemas from `@telemed/shared`
- Sanitize user input before storing
- Rate limiting on auth and payment endpoints
